One more issue in 8513f48: `start_driving` still calls `state.tool_executor.begin_turn(&turn.turn_id)` BEFORE waiting for promotion. For a queued turn B, this runs while turn A is active: `ToolOutcomeBroker::begin_turn` sets active_turn to B and clears the holding area, discarding any early-published socket result that belongs to A (A then waits the full 10 s deadline). Move `begin_turn` to after the receiver is obtained and the Starting transition succeeds (i.e. right before the Prompt is sent). Add a test: A is active with a held (published-before-wait) socket outcome; B is submitted and queued; A's wait_for still gets its outcome immediately. Amend, rerun the same gates, and paste the raw `test result:` lines.
